## Test results and coverage
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
*.trx
TestResults/

## Carve-out: hand-authored .trx FIXTURES for gate-summary.tests.ps1 / local-env.tests.ps1 are
## committed test data, not build output — the *.trx rule above must not eat them (TASK-0022:
## they were silently untracked, so the self-test that guards CI's gate parser was never
## capable of running on a fresh checkout). Scoped to this one directory only, so real test
## output (artifacts/coverage/*.trx, TestResults/*.trx) stays ignored — verify with
## `git check-ignore` after adding a fixture, never assume.
!scripts/tests/fixtures/**/*.trx

## Local secrets and environment — NEVER commit these.
## Real values live in dotnet user-secrets (local) or the secret store (deployed).
## See README.md "Configuration and secrets".
*.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.pem

## Generated OpenAPI documents produced for local inspection.
## The real contract lives in ../contracts/openapi.json and is written only by the
## documented release command — never by hand, never from a developer machine ad hoc.
artifacts/openapi/
*.openapi.local.json

## Local gate runner (TASK-0008) — resolves POSTGRES_TEST_CONNECTION outside the repo tree and
## runs a gate script. Copied from the committed scripts/local-env.template.ps1; see
## README.md "Configuration and secrets". Exact path, not a wildcard, so nothing else under
## scripts/ — including the template itself — is caught by this rule.
scripts/local-env.ps1

